PATCH 290: WIRE the mission-start ACCEPT cascade onto the genuine executed path (retire the FIST_CASCADE
diagnostic gate).  This is the "step 4" that PATCH 172 explicitly deferred ("permanent flow-wiring, held
until the cascade is crash-free end-to-end").  That precondition is now met: with the cascade reconstructed
by patches 154-289 it runs deterministically and crash-free from ACCEPT through the extender MAP-LOAD.

WHAT IT DOES (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin, the pristine FUN_0000_e87a ACCEPT tail 0xe89b..
0xe929): the BATTLES dispatch (e714 _tgt==0xe87a) opens SELECT BATTLE (cb7c) then, on OK (a85d<2), the id=0
mission-BRIEFING modal FUN_0000_7088(0,0x4509).  7088 returns the ACCEPT/CANCEL verdict in the x86 carry
(patch 154: `cmp ds:0x8be2,0xff; cmc` -> 4be2==1 ACCEPT -> CF=0; ==0xff CANCEL -> CF=1), surfaced via the
shim global g_fist_cf.  On ACCEPT (CF==0) the pristine e87a runs the mission-start cascade e43f -> (LOADING
setup) e459 -> 4754 (d501 FSG parse) -> e006/d755/9d26 -> 459a -> 1631 (LOD models) -> e4bb (in-mission
loop).  Patch 172 mirrored that tail faithfully but behind getenv("FIST_CASCADE"); patch 290 removes the
env condition so a real ACCEPT click runs it, exactly as the original does.

EFFECT: the ACCEPT path now POSTS extender op 0x18 (MAP-LOAD) -- verified via FIST_OPHIST (default flow now
shows `FIRST op 0x18`): `[ext] op 0x18 MAP-LOAD: TCB 'D32.KLC'/'C32.KLC'/'532.pal'/'5.SKY'`, tile3918
nz=65536 dist=175, then op 0x54 roster + op 0x0c per-frame render entry.  Crash-free + deterministic (two
serial runs byte-identical ophist; no SIGSEGV).

BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows: NO covered flow clicks ACCEPT.  battles-ok clicks OK then dumps
while the id=0 briefing modal 7088 is STILL OPEN (7088 spins until ACCEPT/CANCEL) -> control never reaches
the cascade block.  battles-cancel-briefing clicks CANCEL (78,186) -> 7088 returns CF=1 -> the `if
(g_fist_cf==0)` block is skipped.  Default boot never opens the briefing.  verify.sh both = 19/19,
native<->wasm bit-identical.  (The in-mission per-frame render loop after the first op 0x0c does not yet
advance frames -- the op-0x4c present pump spins without re-posting ops; that is the documented next
frontier, separate from reaching op 0x18.)

